From 8bcde05bfbbe7a5b2918e47f18850d76fcf8085f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:10:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] TileLang split-K for narrow projections

A narrow projection (512 columns are 8 tiles of 64 on 48 SMs) splits K for
decode rows up to SPLIT_DECODE_ROWS (128), writes FP32 partials and adds them
in shard order; its prefill GEMM accumulates the same shards in the same
order, so a row's bits do not depend on the batch.

- MXFP8: _mxfp8_gemm gains shards, and mxfp8_gemm_partials computes one
  shard per CTA. Shapes listed in SPLIT_FP8 (the DSpark context KV) use them;
  every other projection compiles to the same code as before.
- BF16: TileLangSplitLinearMethod now projects every part in one launch over
  the whole weight: split-K partials plus splitk_reduce_two for decode rows,
  bf16_gemm_two for prefill, shard counts from SPLIT_BF16. No caller changes.
